  "result": "Skip PPO for this project. Training is outside your mission, and it wouldn't be the cheapest or fastest way to improve tool calling for your assistant.\n\nPPO in one line: it nudges a model toward actions that earned higher reward, with a clip that stops any single update from moving too far from the old policy. The objective is `E[min(r·A, clip(r, 1−ε, 1+ε)·A)]`. Here `r` is the new policy's probability of an action divided by the old policy's, and `A` is how much better than average that action was. A real derivation starts from the policy gradient, then adds trust regions. You'd need that background first.\n\nTraining also needs a reward signal, thousands of logged runs and GPUs. That doesn't fit a small sponsor budget.\n\nYour tool-calling gains will come from three cheaper things:\n- clearer tool descriptions\n- a test set of real student requests that you score\n- fixed workflows for the steps that never vary\n\nWant a short lesson on how to write tool descriptions and test them? Or a PPO lesson as an optional extra?",
